WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.990
Speaker 1: Let's now talk about the possible
outcomes to the 2022 midterm election.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:12.490
There are four possible outcomes to the midterms
that are now just a few weeks away.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.180
Three of the outcomes are really pretty bad.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.200
So let's explore what these outcomes are.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.470
We have control of the house up for grabs
and control of the Senate up for grabs.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:31.119
If we look at the latest FiveThirtyEight forecasts,
Democrats are by a roughly 2 to 1 margin favored

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:36.840
to win the Senate, roughly by a 2 to 1 margin
favored to win in the Senate.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:42.649
And if you look at the House, Republicans
are by a greater than 2 to 1 margin favored

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:44.630
to win the House.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:50.580
So if we want to put numbers to this, there's
a roughly 70% chance that Republicans win

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.770
the House and a roughly 67% chance that Democrats
win the Senate.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:59.050
So you essentially have four possible outcomes.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.120
Imagine a two by two grid.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.370
Democrats could win both the House and Senate.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.649
Republicans could win both the House and Senate.

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:09.259
You could have Democrats win the House but
lose the Senate.

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:11.450
You could have Democrats win the Senate but
lose the House.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.060
Those are the four scenarios.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:16.060
So let's do some simple probability math.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.740
These should add up to 100%.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.409
These are the four possible outcomes, and
we're going to do these in order of likelihood.

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:24.329
And then you have the following.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:29.610
Based on the FiveThirtyEight projections,
the most likely outcome is Democrats win the

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.369
Senate and Republicans win the House.

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:32.990
That's 46%.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.509
You've got a 24% chance that the Republicans
win both.

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:39.420
You've got a 20% chance that Democrats win
both.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.119
And then you've got a 10% chance that Democrats
win the House, but Republicans win the Senate.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:44.479
That's the least likely outcome.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:47.640
So let's start with the least likely and work
up.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.099
If Democrats win the House and Republicans
win the Senate, it's not going to happen.

00:01:53.099 --> 00:01:59.060
But it would mean that Democrats pass a ton
of stuff in the House that Joe Biden wants,

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.109
and basically none of it gets passed the Senate.

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:03.259
It's a done deal.

00:02:03.259 --> 00:02:05.829
It's really good for Republicans in 2024.

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:10.660
They can say, look, they had the House and
the White House.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.970
They proposed nothing reasonable.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:18.890
The Senate had to block the stuff they wanted
to do, vote for Republicans in 2024.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:19.910
Okay.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.920
Next scenario is that Democrats win both.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.160
This is the best outcome, quite frankly.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.000
There's only a 20% chance of that.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:33.500
Now, in this scenario, the Senate margin is
not 6040, meaning that it remains like the

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.400
last two years.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.420
A lot of stuff.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.920
You need 60 votes in order to pass.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.670
So Democrats, if they held both the House
and Senate, would be able to get some things

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.670
done.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.790
Republicans would obstruct in the Senate for
everything that require 60 votes.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:52.680
They would claim these Democrats are so extreme
in what they propose, we have no choice.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.400
Next scenario, in order of likelihood going
up is Republicans take the House and the Senate.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.040
Now, that's also not the most likely scenario.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.290
It's obviously disastrous.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.780
Nothing will get done for two years if Republicans
take both.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.460
They will try to blame Biden, even though
it is their obstruction that will prevent

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.600
anything from getting done.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.450
They will say We had no choice.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:18.120
Everything Biden and the Democrats put forward
was so extreme that we had to block it.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:23.350
It will give them a good setup for 2024, including
to actually try to influence the election

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:28.540
itself by all sorts of subterfuge and arguably
illegal means.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:35.510
The most likely outcome, a plurality, is that
Democrats win the Senate and Republicans win

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:36.510
the House.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:41.880
There's a nearly 50% chance of that particular
individual result.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:47.400
In that scenario, Republicans will stop things
in the House.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.400
Democrats will control the Senate, but will
have no super majority.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.100
And it will mean that almost nothing happens.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:59.400
Biden will be blamed, Democrats will be blamed,
and then Republicans will use it to their

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.180
advantage in 2024.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.870
So what has to happen?

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:12.450
Obviously we should not concede the House,
but the math of it is very much not in the

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.350
favor of Democrats.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:23.300
So the scenario that is the most likely is
Democrats keep the Senate by a small margin,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.120
but lose the House.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:32.009
What we need to see is some of the gubernatorial
races go to the Democratic candidate, because

00:04:32.009 --> 00:04:37.509
ultimately you are going to have, I believe,
very little accomplished during the next two

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:40.719
years thanks to Republicans taking the House.

00:04:40.719 --> 00:04:47.400
And then you will have a 2024 election, which
may come down to governors in key states potentially

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.850
stealing electoral votes.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:58.020
Pennsylvania is a huge issue where Josh SHAPIRO
has to beat off a challenge from Doug Mastriano,

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.059
who he will try to steal the Pennsylvania
electoral votes for the Republican nominee.

00:05:02.059 --> 00:05:03.059
We know that.

00:05:03.059 --> 00:05:06.180
So Josh SHAPIRO has got to win in Pennsylvania
and Arizona.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:11.610
This radical big lie purveyor, Carrie Lake,
is currently winning by a little bit.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:15.849
Arizona is another important state where if
you have a Republican governor who is a full

00:05:15.849 --> 00:05:22.310
big lie proponent, she may try to steal the
Arizona electoral votes for the Republican

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:26.110
candidate, even if they don't actually win
the popular vote in that state.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:31.740
So I believe that the most likely scenario
here is Democrats keep the Senate, lose the

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:38.569
House, and the next two years will ultimately
conclude with do Democrats control enough

00:05:38.569 --> 00:05:46.819
governors houses that they can prevent the
theft of the 2024 election if the Democratic

00:05:46.819 --> 00:05:48.370
candidate is to win?

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.650
It's also possible that the next two years
are so disastrous that a Republican president

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:55.120
legitimately wins in 2024.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.530
We can't deal with that now.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:59.839
What we can deal with is who do we vote for
in just three and a half weeks?

00:05:59.839 --> 00:06:03.199
I think roughly three, two and a half weeks,
three and a half weeks.

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:05.559
And these are the four scenarios.

00:06:05.559 --> 00:06:06.559
Let me know your thoughts.

00:06:06.559 --> 00:06:11.690
We will have this and all of our other clips
on our Instagram, which you can find at David

